Presentation Script & Slide Content – HairCoaction Internship (Pankaj Kumar)

Slide 1 – Title
- HairCoaction: Building a Modern Web App with Automated CI/CD
- Intern: Pankaj Kumar | Duration: 6 Weeks

Slide 2 – Problem & Goals
- Need: A responsive, production-ready site for HairCoaction
- Goals: Launch quickly, add auth + feature modules, and automate deploys for continuous iteration

Slide 3 – Tech Stack
- Frontend: Vite + React + TypeScript + Tailwind CSS
- Auth: Firebase Authentication (email/password + Google)
- Routing: react-router-dom
- DevOps: GitHub Actions (CI) + Netlify (CD)

Slide 4 – Architecture Overview
- Public Landing Page → Authentication → Dashboard (tabbed sections)
- Feature modules: Education, Consultation, Events, Community, Profile
- API stubs (Node/Express) prepared for future backend

Slide 5 – Key Features
- Responsive UI with rich animations and dark/light theme
- Authentication flows and protected routes
- Modular components for rapid iteration

Slide 6 – DevOps Pipeline
- CI: Lint, Typecheck, Build on every push/PR (.github/workflows/ci.yml)
- CD: Auto-deploy to Netlify on main (.github/workflows/deploy-netlify.yml)
- Secrets required: NETLIFY_SITE_ID, NETLIFY_AUTH_TOKEN (GitHub repo → Settings → Secrets)

Slide 7 – Demo Flow
- Visit Landing Page → Sign Up / Login → Dashboard tabs → Feature previews
- Emphasis: Fast builds, safe merges, automatic deployments

Slide 8 – Results
- Shipped a polished MVP with auth and feature scaffolding
- Reliable CI prevents regressions; CD enables immediate demos

Slide 9 – Lessons Learned
- Importance of early CI to catch integration issues
- Consistent theming/state management (moved Landing page darkMode control to App)
- Planning API stubs eases future backend adoption

Slide 10 – Next Steps
- Connect database (Supabase) and wire real data
- Add tests (Vitest, Playwright) and quality gates
- Observability: Sentry; Security: Semgrep

